From: GPT-6.1-Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l45: allow hardware readback of restored operating point

The bypassed reads introduced in 0198 still obey regmap's readable policy.
Without these entries even a healthy restoration fails with -EIO. Allow
only the four operating-point registers already written by 0122. All four
are explicitly readable in the retained ASUS WW33 CS35L45 driver's
cs35l45-tables.c; no expansion to unknown/reserved register ranges.

Local correction, using vendor register access policy rather than an
upstream backport. Hardware: verify direct I2C readback and healthy DSP
shutdown/restart, then the 0198 fault/reset-latch cases on both speakers.

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45-tables.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45-tables.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45-tables.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45-tables.c
@@ -124,6 +124,11 @@
 	case CS35L45_GLOBAL_ENABLES:
 	case CS35L45_BLOCK_ENABLES:
 	case CS35L45_BLOCK_ENABLES2:
+	/* Vendor operating-point registers verified after restoration. */
+	case CS35L45_BOOST_LPMODE_CFG:
+	case CS35L45_BST_BPE_IL_LIM_THLD:
+	case CS35L45_LDPM_CONFIG:
+	case CS35L45_MIXER_PILOT0_INPUT:
 	case CS35L45_ERROR_RELEASE:
 	case CS35L45_SYNC_GPIO1:
 	case CS35L45_INTB_GPIO2_MCLK_REF:
